---
import MarketingLayout from '@/layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import SEO from '@/components/common/SEO.astro';
import { siteConfig, company } from '@/config';
---

<SEO
  title="Landed Cost Methodology — How We Calculate Chinese EV Import Costs"
  description="Transparent methodology for EV Hub landed-cost estimates: EU import duty, countervailing duty, VAT, RoRo freight, certification, and registration."
/>

<MarketingLayout title="Landed Cost Methodology">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <div class="mb-10">
      <a href="/" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-green-600">← Back to home</a>
    </div>

    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-3">Landed Cost Methodology</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-600 mb-10">
      How EV Hub estimates the real cost of importing a Chinese EV — the exact formula, data
      sources, and assumptions behind every number on this site.
    </p>

    <div class="prose max-w-none space-y-8">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Why we publish this</h2>
        <p>
          Most Chinese EV listings show only the factory or FOB price. A car advertised at $14,000
          can land in Germany at over $28,000 once duties, VAT, freight, and certification are
          applied. That gap is the single biggest surprise for first-time importers — and the reason
          EV Hub exists.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every landed-cost figure on EV Hub is produced from a single, documented formula using
          public tariff schedules, national tax rates, and industry freight benchmarks. This page is
          that documentation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">The formula</h2>
        <p class="font-mono text-sm bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg">
          landed_price = base_price × (1 + std_duty) × (1 + countervailing_duty) × (1 + VAT)<br/>
          &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;+ RoRo freight + customs clearance + certification + registration + inland transport
        </p>
        <p>
          Duties compound in this order because that is how customs valuations cascade in practice:
          the standard duty is assessed on the CIF value, the countervailing duty on top of that,
          and VAT is charged last on the duty-inclusive total.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">1. Standard import duty — 10%</h2>
        <p>
          All passenger EVs imported into the EU are subject to a <strong>10% most-favoured-nation
          (MFN) import duty</strong>, assessed on the CIF value (car price + insurance + freight).
          <span class="text-gray-600">[Source: EU Common Customs Tariff, TARIC]</span>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">2. Countervailing duty — 17% to 35.3%</h2>
        <p>
          Since 2024, the EU applies <strong>anti-subsidy (countervailing) duties</strong> to Chinese
          battery-electric vehicles, on top of the standard 10%. Rates are set per producer:
        </p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead><tr class="border-b border-gray-300"><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Producer</th><th class="text-left py-2">Rate</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200"><td class="py-2">BYD</td><td class="py-2">17.0%</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200"><td class="py-2">Geely (incl. Zeekr, Polestar)</td><td class="py-2">18.8%</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200"><td class="py-2">SAIC (MG)</td><td class="py-2">35.3%</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200"><td class="py-2">Other / non-cooperating producers</td><td class="py-2">18.8% – 35.3%</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
          [Source: EU Commission Implementing Regulation on countervailing duties for BEVs from China]
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">3. VAT, 19% to 23% by destination</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-sm">
            <thead><tr class="border-b border-gray-300"><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Country</th><th class="text-left py-2">VAT</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200"><td class="py-2">Germany</td><td class="py-2">19%</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200"><td class="py-2">France</td><td class="py-2">20%</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200"><td class="py-2">Netherlands</td><td class="py-2">21%</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200"><td class="py-2">United Kingdom</td><td class="py-2">20%</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200"><td class="py-2">Italy</td><td class="py-2">22%</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200"><td class="py-2">Spain</td><td class="py-2">21%</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">[Source: national tax authorities]</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">4. Freight & fixed costs</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>RoRo ocean freight</strong>: $1,500 – $2,500 per vehicle (China → North Europe main ports). We use $2,000 as the central estimate.</li>
          <li><strong>Customs clearance</strong>: ~$350 per vehicle.</li>
          <li><strong>Certification / homologation</strong>: $1,500 – $5,000 (ECWVTA or Small Series approval). We use $3,250 central.</li>
          <li><strong>Registration</strong>: $400 – $500 (Germany ~$500).</li>
          <li><strong>Inland transport</strong>: ~$500 from port to dealer/registrant.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">[Source: industry freight and homologation benchmarks]</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Assumptions & limits</h2>
        <p>
          These are <strong>B2B import estimates</strong>, not retail quotes. Actual landed cost varies
          with trim, port of entry, volume, currency, and homologation route. Figures are refreshed
          when tariff schedules or tax rates change, and every estimate on the site carries its data
          date.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-8 text-sm text-gray-600">
        <p>
          Published by <strong>{company.name}</strong> · Author: <strong>{company.author}</strong>, {company.authorRole}
          <br/>Last reviewed: {siteConfig.legal.lastUpdated}
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>
